# An operator at the start of a line without a pipe: one error, then it parses as an operator.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where x > 1
project a
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..31
  PIPELINE@0..30
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..20
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..20
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "x"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        GT@17..18 ">"
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        LITERAL@19..20
          LONG@19..20 "1"
    WHITESPACE@20..21 "\n"
    PROJECT_OP@21..30
      IDENT@21..28 "project"
      WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@29..30
        NAME_REF@29..30
          IDENT@29..30 "a"
  WHITESPACE@30..31 "\n"

error[DS0102]: missing `|` before `project`
  --> query:2:1
  |
2 | project a
  | ^^^^^^^ `project` starts a new operator
  |
  = help: insert `|` to pipe into `project`: `| project`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | where x > 1
    | project a
which parses without errors
